<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Barony of Kalavryta</h1><p class="st-meta">1209 CE – 1270 CE (approx.) · capital Kalavryta</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Short-lived Frankish barony in the mountains of northern Peloponnese, one of the first lost to the reviving Byzantines.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kalavryta was one of the twelve baronies set up in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-achaea">Principality of Achaea</a> around 1209. It was granted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otho-of-tournay">Otho of Tournay</a> and covered the mountainous district around the town of Kalavryta in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>, with twelve knight's fiefs.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Like other baronies, it was held by a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knighthood">knightly</a> family owing military service and counsel to the prince and governing a Greek peasant population from a castle. Records say little more about it than the name of its lords.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the Principality ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mystras">Mistras</a> and other forts to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a> in 1262, Byzantine forces pushed north. Kalavryta was taken around 1270 and the barony ceased to exist, though the area later changed hands again before passing permanently to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/despotate-of-the-morea">Despotate of the Morea</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/barony-of-kalavryta.jpg" alt="Barony of Kalavryta" width="320" height="251"><figcaption>Image: Peloponnese_Middle_Ages_map-fr.svg: Eric Gaba (Sting - fr:Sting) derivative work: Constantine ✍ · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peloponnese_Middle_Ages_map-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1209 CE – 1270 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kalavryta</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Otho of Tournay</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity (rulers), Eastern Orthodox Christianity (population)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French, Medieval Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kalavryta</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1240&amp;focus=barony-of-kalavryta" aria-label="Barony of Kalavryta on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5231 811 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Barony of Kalavryta lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5551 1067L5530 1071M5551 1067L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5530 1071h0M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5551 1067h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5551 1067h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1240&amp;focus=barony-of-kalavryta">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

